// MathNet Problem: 048d
@Competition: CroatianCompetitions2011
@Topic: Geometry > Plane Geometry > Miscellaneous > Angle chasing

// State space for mathematical reasoning
State(4096) → reasoning_space
WaveState(2048) → solution_wave

// Problem: Outside a regular polygon $A_1A_2\dots A_n$ a point $B$ is given so that $A_1A_2B$ is a regular triangle. Determine all $n$ such that points $B$, $A_2$ and $A_3$ are consecutive vertices of some regul...

// Apply reasoning transform
reasoning_space @ W_initial >> LayerNorm

// Attention over solution candidates
Attention(query=reasoning_space, memory=solution_wave)

// Entropy gate to collapse to correct solution
⊕EntropyGate(threshold=0.3)

// Answer: n ∈ {3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 15, 18, 24, 42}
